+* `SCCACHE_CACHE_READ_TIMEOUT_SECS` how long, in seconds, a cache lookup may take before sccache gives up on it and compiles locally. Defaults to `60`. A lower value helps when the storage backend is slow or unresponsive rather than failing outright, for example in CI. In a multi-level chain the deadline is shared: each level is tried with its share of the remaining time, so one stalled level cannot consume the whole lookup budget before the later levels are tried.
+* `SCCACHE_BACKEND_BACKOFF_THRESHOLD` how many consecutive timed-out reads a cache level tolerates before its reads are skipped for a cooldown window (default `3`, `0` disables the skip). Evaluated per level, so in a `disk,s3` chain a stalled `s3` trips only its own gate and the local disk keeps serving; any read the level answers resets its counter. Reads only — writes never skip.
